
enum Noun {
    Baba,
    Key,
}

enum Verb {
    Is,
}

enum Property {
    You,
    Win,
}

enum Text {
    Noun(Noun),
    Verb(Verb),
    Property(Property),
    Not,
    And,
    ...etc
}

enum UnitKind {
    Object(Noun),
    Text(Text),
}

struct Unit {
    id: Guid,
    kind: UnitKind,
    slug: String, // e.g. "baba", "key", "you" used for level loading/saving
}

Note ^ no prototype for the unit yet until we go data-driven

struct Cell {
    units: Vec<Unit>
}

struct Rule {
    ...
}

struct World {
    grid: Vec<Cell>,
}


Pipeline:
1. parse rules from the grid U->D and L->R in a maximal run to create a Vec<Rule>
2. read input
3. do movements: YOU, MOVE, AUTO, NUDGE...
4. reparse
5. object transformations via IS
6. reparse
7. additional "acted on by entity" movements: TELE, SHIFT...
8. reparse
9. cleanup: remove stacks of same object beyond a certain depth (retail game allows 6)
10. object falling: FALL_LEFT, FALL_RIGHT, ...
11. reparse
12. entity status updates: LEFT, TURN, FLOAT, ...
13. object falling again
14. level updates: (this is completely out of scope for now)
15. block updates: HOT, MELT, DEFEAT, OPEN, SHUT, ...
16. reparse
17. check for win conditions and no-YOU state

vertical slice for a playable level 1:
1. parse -> Vec<Rule>
2. snapshot
3. input
4. move YOU and do push chains
5. reparse
6. transformations
7. reparse
8. check win conditions
